    "title": "Legendary Pianist's Death Latest Blow to Denver Jazz Scene - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Roberts ,\n5 days ago Pianist Purnell Steen, who died on November 18 at age 84 after injuring himself in a fall, was among the most revered performers in Denver jazz — and his loss is the second in recent months to strike a family whose roots may run deeper than any other on the local music scene, regardless of genre. Steen’s cousin, legendary bassist Charles Burrell, was 104 years old when he passed away in June. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
